// @trap
// @hint redundant type annotation: `k` is inferred as `i32` — `--fix` keeps a return annotation as the signature's documentation; remove it by hand if it is not
// `u as! i32` over a type parameter pinned at no number is never the target, so it traps, the
// `as!` twin of `as?` answering `null` there (D2791). A `boolean` pin is a number's source and
// converts, pinned in `as-type-param-boolean-pin.vl`.
function k<T>(u: T): i32 { u as! i32 }
print(k("s"))
print(-1)
